```ts
/** A fenced code block or an inline code span, in that order of greed. */
const INLINE_CODE = /`[^`\n]*`/g;
```

Approach: build a mask that replaces code with spaces, then for escaping walk segments.

Simplest clean implementation: a single function that yields segments of {text, code} covering the whole text, handling fences via fenceSegments then inline spans within prose.

```ts
